    "body": "## Description\n\nCreate `docs/glossary.md` — a glossary of browser terminology that contributors will encounter as they work on the project. This helps new contributors who are unfamiliar with terms like \"reflow\", \"DOM\", or \"cascade\".\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `docs/glossary.md`.\n2. Define at least 15 terms, each with a one or two sentence explanation. Suggested terms:\n   - DOM\n   - CSSOM\n   - Reflow\n   - Repaint\n   - Cascade\n   - Selector specificity\n   - Tokenizer\n   - Parse tree\n   - Render tree\n   - Layout\n   - Compositing\n   - Paint\n   - Event loop\n   - IPC\n   - Origin\n3. Alphabetize the terms.\n4. Link to it from `README.md`.\n5. Commit with `docs: add browser glossary`.\n6. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Building vocabulary around browser internals.\n- Technical writing and research.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [MDN: Web technology glossary](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary)\n- [Web.dev: How browsers work](https://web.dev/articles/howbrowserswork)\n",
